WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.455
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online IELTS preparation.

2
00:00:05.755 --> 00:00:09.350
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:18.038
Unit ten: Reading: Multiple Choice and Time Management. Today you will choose answers wisely and finish all three passages in sixty minutes.

4
00:00:18.338 --> 00:00:20.851
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:24.812
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:26.430
Stem.

7
00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:30.740
Stem means the question part of a multiple choice item.

8
00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:32.943
Read the stem carefully.

9
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:35.924
Your turn. Say: Stem.

10
00:00:38.767 --> 00:00:39.745
Stem.

11
00:00:40.483 --> 00:00:41.229
Trap.

12
00:00:42.217 --> 00:00:44.890
Trap means an option that looks right but is wrong.

13
00:00:45.483 --> 00:00:46.984
This option is a trap.

14
00:00:47.583 --> 00:00:50.468
Your turn. Say: Trap.

15
00:00:53.333 --> 00:00:54.044
Trap.

16
00:00:54.783 --> 00:00:55.715
Pace.

17
00:00:56.717 --> 00:00:58.565
Pace means the speed you work at.

18
00:00:59.150 --> 00:01:00.546
Keep a steady pace.

19
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:03.814
Your turn. Say: Pace.

20
00:01:06.667 --> 00:01:07.540
Pace.

21
00:01:08.283 --> 00:01:09.099
Skip.

22
00:01:10.083 --> 00:01:12.559
Skip means to leave a question and come back.

23
00:01:13.150 --> 00:01:14.697
Skip a hard question.

24
00:01:15.283 --> 00:01:17.483
Your turn. Say: Skip.

25
00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:21.323
Skip.

26
00:01:22.083 --> 00:01:22.922
Review.

27
00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:26.183
Review means to check your answers again.

28
00:01:26.783 --> 00:01:28.678
Review your answers at the end.

29
00:01:29.283 --> 00:01:31.878
Your turn. Say: Review.

30
00:01:34.733 --> 00:01:35.781
Review.

31
00:01:36.517 --> 00:01:37.680
Prioritise.

32
00:01:38.683 --> 00:01:41.983
Prioritise means to decide what is most important first.

33
00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:44.525
Prioritise easier questions.

34
00:01:45.117 --> 00:01:48.094
Your turn. Say: Prioritise.

35
00:01:50.933 --> 00:01:52.120
Prioritise.

36
00:01:52.883 --> 00:01:53.954
Allocate.

37
00:01:54.950 --> 00:01:57.797
Allocate means to give a fixed amount of time.

38
00:01:58.383 --> 00:02:00.603
Allocate twenty minutes per passage.

39
00:02:01.217 --> 00:02:03.857
Your turn. Say: Allocate.

40
00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.701
Allocate.

41
00:02:08.450 --> 00:02:09.265
Transfer.

42
00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:13.480
Transfer means to copy answers onto the answer sheet.

43
00:02:14.083 --> 00:02:16.884
There is no extra time to transfer answers.

44
00:02:17.483 --> 00:02:20.310
Your turn. Say: Transfer.

45
00:02:23.167 --> 00:02:24.075
Transfer.

46
00:02:24.867 --> 00:02:28.831
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:29.683 --> 00:02:32.507
Visal, how long should I spend on each passage?

48
00:02:33.617 --> 00:02:42.399
About twenty minutes each. In Reading there is no extra time to transfer answers, so write your answers directly on the answer sheet.

49
00:02:43.483 --> 00:02:45.494
How do I answer multiple choice?

50
00:02:46.583 --> 00:02:57.258
Read the stem first, find the part of the text, and then read every option. Eliminate options that are too extreme or only partly true.

51
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.222
What if I am running out of time?

52
00:03:01.317 --> 00:03:12.923
Never leave blanks. Guess if necessary, because there is no negative marking. Prioritise questions you can answer quickly and return to harder ones later.

53
00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.648
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:16.483 --> 00:03:20.979
Grammar focus: Strategy: pace yourself and never leave a blank.

55
00:03:21.279 --> 00:03:22.489
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:23.183 --> 00:03:25.914
Allocate about twenty minutes to each passage.

57
00:03:26.817 --> 00:03:30.384
There is no negative marking, so never leave a blank.

58
00:03:31.333 --> 00:03:39.106
Plan twenty minutes per passage, skip hard questions and return to them. Write answers directly on the sheet and always guess if you run out of time.

59
00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:43.512
Be careful! Don't say: I leave hard questions blank.

60
00:03:45.467 --> 00:03:47.756
Say: I guess if I run out of time.

61
00:03:48.056 --> 00:03:49.394
No negative marking.

62
00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:52.585
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:53.400 --> 00:03:54.715
Finishing in Time.

64
00:03:55.015 --> 00:03:58.361
Sokha practises three passages in sixty minutes.

65
00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.622
He spends twenty minutes on each one.

66
00:04:02.633 --> 00:04:06.189
When a question is too hard, he skips it and returns later.

67
00:04:07.200 --> 00:04:09.629
He remembers that there is no negative marking.

68
00:04:10.633 --> 00:04:13.620
At the end he has no blanks, and his score improves.

69
00:04:14.733 --> 00:04:18.793
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.905
How much time is suggested per passage?

71
00:04:22.205 --> 00:04:26.392
A, forty minutes. B, twenty minutes. C, five minutes.

72
00:04:29.933 --> 00:04:32.258
The answer is B: twenty minutes.

73
00:04:33.417 --> 00:04:36.066
In Reading, you should write answers blank.

74
00:04:36.366 --> 00:04:41.947
A, after the test. B, on the question paper only. C, directly on the sheet.

75
00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:48.312
The answer is C: directly on the sheet.

76
00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.519
Is there negative marking in IELTS?

77
00:04:51.819 --> 00:04:55.136
A, no. B, yes. C, only in Reading.

78
00:04:58.700 --> 00:05:00.386
The answer is A: no.

79
00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.875
What should you do with a very hard question?

80
00:05:04.175 --> 00:05:09.186
A, stop the test. B, skip and return. C, leave it blank.

81
00:05:12.733 --> 00:05:15.360
The answer is B: skip and return.

82
00:05:16.517 --> 00:05:18.423
What happened to Sokha's score?

83
00:05:18.723 --> 00:05:23.364
A, it stayed zero. B, it was cancelled. C, it improved.

84
00:05:26.900 --> 00:05:29.515
The answer is C: it improved.

85
00:05:30.700 --> 00:05:34.049
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:34.883 --> 00:05:37.092
How do you manage your time in the Reading test?

87
00:05:45.883 --> 00:05:47.453
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:47.753 --> 00:06:03.411
I give each passage about twenty minutes. If a question is difficult, I skip it and come back later. I write my answers directly on the answer sheet, and I never leave a blank because there is no negative marking.

89
00:06:03.711 --> 00:06:05.374
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:06:06.283 --> 00:06:12.465
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: pace yourself and never leave a blank.

91
00:06:12.765 --> 00:06:17.066
Today's value is time management. Plan your day and use your time well.

92
00:06:17.366 --> 00:06:19.821
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:20.121 --> 00:06:23.470
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

